WEBVTT

NOTE English translation; original display timings, not word alignment.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.833
This classroom is a little different.
The teacher and students are all AI.

2
00:00:03.833 --> 00:00:06.167
And you can join their discussion.

3
00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:09.600
We made this video
to introduce an open-source project.

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.900
Your project could reach
more people this way, too.

5
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.833
How? Give Codex your GitHub link.

6
00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:19.400
Then tell it who you want
the video to reach.

7
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.867
It reads the project materials
and finds what is worth telling.

8
00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:25.500
Then, a script and storyboard.

9
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Review them first.
Then video production begins.

10
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.467
Take that classroom.

11
00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.100
Leave technical details for later.

12
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.700
Show the AI teacher and students in action.
Easier to follow, right?

13
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.667
Once you see the video,
maybe the pace feels too slow.

14
00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:44.633
Or a key point is still unclear.
Just say so, and keep refining it.

15
00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:48.500
At the end, you get more than
a video with narration and subtitles.

16
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.000
Keep the script and project files to edit later.

17
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.667
You build the project.
We help you explain it.

18
00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:57.367
Start with your GitHub link.
